terminology, these are classified as packing/dressings rather than sinus stents. Stents typically provide structural    
support to maintain ostial patency, while spacers/packing primarily prevent synechiae formation.                        
                                                                                                                        
- Study 5: Excluded because the stent released doxycycline (antibiotic/MMP inhibitor), not a corticosteroid. The        
protocol specifically requires "steroid-eluting" stents.                                                                
                                                                                                                        
