  Test SNOT-20 data were collected at each visit. A small sample underwent endoscopic mucosal biopsy. RESULTS           
  Twenty-nine of 30 patients completed the protocol. The difference in edema, crusting, and mucopurulence at 1 and 2    
  weeks was not statistically significant; however, at 6 and 12 weeks, the HA hydrogel showed statistically             
  significant reduction in both overall endoscopic grade (p < 0.05), as well as synechiae formation (p < 0.05), with a  
  trend toward superiority in remucosalization (p = 0.08). Histological analysis of six subjects at 12 weeks showed a   
